WEBVTT

00:05:58.396 --> 00:06:01.232
to looking for each other under rubble,

00:06:01.232 --> 00:06:03.234
wondering if we had all made it alive.

00:06:03.859 --> 00:06:06.112
Luckily, we did,

00:06:06.112 --> 00:06:10.074
and we were much luckier
than a lot of people in the same street.

00:06:10.366 --> 00:06:12.660
My cinematographer, Joe,
almost lost his eye

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:13.994
and everyone was injured.

00:06:15.579 --> 00:06:17.581
We got out of the street

00:06:17.581 --> 00:06:22.670
and realized that the explosion
was not just next to the office,

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:23.671
but everywhere,

00:06:23.671 --> 00:06:25.965
and that’s when we understood
how big it was.

00:06:26.549 --> 00:06:29.093
Walking down the street like zombies
around that time,

00:06:29.093 --> 00:06:33.389
surrounded by broken,
confused, stunned faces,